course: dictionary
lesson: 9239
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «The chimney was sooty after years of coal smoke.» Here sooty means covered with soot, the black powder that smoke leaves behind. Ask yourself: is the thing covered in soot, or is it just very dark?
explain: Sooty can also mean black or very dark, like soot. In «Nobody chooses the change and no animal tries to change: dark moths were simply eaten less often on sooty trees, so more dark moths were left to have young.» the trees are dark, the colour of soot, so the dark moths were hard to spot. Check by swapping in another word: black trees still fits.
explain: A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a clue. «Connor's cat Sooty avoids him because he plays his drum kit next to her basket» uses Sooty as a name, not a description. Sooty is also the name of a famous yellow glove-puppet bear with black ears on a British children's TV show.
fact: Sooty is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a sooty chimney, a sooty face, sooty black.
fact: «Sooty» means covered with soot, the black powder left by smoke from burning coal, wood or oil.
fact: «Sooty» can also mean black or very dark, like soot.
fact: The forms are sooty, sootier and sootiest: «sootier» means more covered in soot, and «sootiest» means the most.
fact: «Sooty» is also a name: the yellow glove-puppet bear on a long-running British children's TV show.
exercise: «The chimney was sooty after years of coal smoke.» What does sooty mean here? | Wet with rain | Very loud | Shiny and clean | *Covered with soot, the black powder from smoke
exercise: «Dark moths were eaten less often on sooty trees.» What colour are the sooty trees? | Bright pink | Bare and white | Shiny gold | *Dark, like soot
exercise: In «Connor's cat Sooty avoids him», what kind of word is Sooty? | A type of smoke | A colour | *A name, with a capital letter | A verb that means to hide
test: Which word best fits? The ___ face after the bonfire made everyone laugh. | barely | *sooty | glum | ancient
test: Which word is the name of a yellow glove-puppet bear on a British children's TV show? | Tern | Soot | *Sooty | Sootiest
exam: Which word completes this sentence? The old chimney was ___ than the new one. | soots | sooty | sootiest | *sootier
